- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`

**How to implement.** The ensemble statistics move into Optimization (001 §Q AT-2 '`RecoveredQuantity`, `RecoveryStatistics`, `statisticsFor`'; the S10.1 brief 'RecoveredQuantity, RecoveryStatistics, NoisyExperiment, statisticsFor, standardErrorOfMean, rowFor'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. Names are `ParameterName`s and values `QuantityValue`s (step 338), because a bare `string` or `double` in a record field or beside our types is ELEV008 / ELEV010. Errors are values (AGENTS.md: 'do not throw across a public boundary'): what the harness `failwith`s becomes an `Error` of `MuellerFitError`, and the tests unwrap it with `expectOk`. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs`, `module RecoveryEnsembles` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, compiled directly after `BenchNoise.fs` (one `<Compile>` line, no comment). Its module doc, one to three lines: what an ensemble of noisy experiments says about each recovered quantity, moved by spec 0050 S10.1 (specs/0044/.manual/011-noisy-measurement-tests.md). Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (2) In it: `RecoveredQuantity<'Parameters>` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:RecoveredQuantity`) becomes `{ name : ParameterName; valueIn : 'Parameters -> QuantityValue }`, `ofAxis axis` reading `QuantityValue (axis.read p)` and `derived (name : ParameterName) (valueIn : 'Parameters -> QuantityValue)`. `RecoveryStatistics<'Parameters>` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:RecoveryStatistics`) keeps its fields with `mean` and `absoluteScatter` as `QuantityValue`; `describe` renders the same text from their values. `NoisyExperiment<'Parameters>` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:NoisyExperiment`) is `{ seed : NoiseSeed; fit : MuellerFitData<'Parameters> }`. New `type EnsembleSize = | EnsembleSize of int` with `value`, doc one line: how many experiments an ensemble holds. `statisticsFor` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:statisticsFor`) keeps its signature and runs today's arithmetic on the same doubles in the same order (the mean by `List.average`, the Bessel-corrected variance, `bias` as `RelativeError.between` of the mean and the truth, `scatter` as `sqrt variance / abs truth`, `worst` the `List.max` of the per-experiment `RelativeError`s), its `mean` and `absoluteScatter` born as `QuantityValue`s. `standardErrorOfMean (size : EnsembleSize) (row : RecoveryStatistics<'Parameters>) : RelativeError` is `row.scatter.value / sqrt (float size.value) |> RelativeError`. `rowFor (table : RecoveryStatistics<'Parameters> list) (name : ParameterName) : Result<RecoveryStatistics<'Parameters>, MuellerFitError>` answers the row whose `quantity.name` is `name`, and `Error (UnknownQuantityErr name)` when none is. (3) `MuellerFitError` gains `UnknownQuantityErr of ParameterName` (no ensemble row of that name). (4) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes the three types and the three functions. (5) Callers, test code only. `BiaxialSample.recoveredQuantities`, `MuellerInverseTests.recoveredQuantities` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.reportedQuantities` pass `RecoveredQuantity.derived (ParameterName "<name>") (fun p -> QuantityValue (<today's expression>))`. In `MuellerInverseTests`, `BiaxialInverseTests` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` every `rowFor table <name>` becomes `(rowFor table (ParameterName <name>) |> expectOk)`, and `rowFor table name.value` (`observedScatter`, whose `name` is already a `ParameterName`) becomes `(rowFor table name |> expectOk)`; every `absoluteScatter` compared as a number reads `.value`, and `standardErrorOfMean (List.length <seeds>) row` becomes `standardErrorOfMean (EnsembleSize (List.length <seeds>)) row`. Every band, message and assertion keeps its text. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the statistics are the same operations on the same doubles. No test is added or removed. `MuellerInverseTests`' ensemble fact is the cheapest that drives all six (`BiaxialInverseTests` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests`, at about 1000 s each, are not selected).

**Acceptance.** After the move, `RecoveryEnsembles.fs` MUST declare `RecoveredQuantity` (named by `ParameterName`, valued in `QuantityValue`), `RecoveryStatistics`, `NoisyExperiment`, `EnsembleSize`, `statisticsFor`, `standardErrorOfMean` and `rowFor` (an unknown name being `UnknownQuantityErr`), compiled directly after `BenchNoise.fs`, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare none of them; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.
